intro="Reproduction does not keep an individual alive, but it keeps the **species** alive. Organisms make copies of themselves using DNA copying and a little variation, so that populations survive environmental changes. This chapter compares asexual and sexual reproduction, follows flowering plants from pollination to seed and explains the human reproductive systems.",
big_questions=["Why is variation useful for a species?", "How do plants and animals reproduce with one or two parents?", "How does the human reproductive system work?"],
