("h2", "7.1 DNA Copying and Variation"),
("p", "Cells copy their **DNA** and create extra cell machinery before dividing, so daughter cells carry the same blueprint. The copying is never perfectly accurate, so **variations** appear. Variations help a population: some individuals survive when conditions change, such as heat or a new disease. Bacteria reproduce rapidly; a heat-resistant variant survives a heat wave."),
("h2", "7.2 Modes of Asexual Reproduction"),
